def tbl(rows,widths):
 t=Table([[Paragraph(str(x),st['SmallAA']) for x in row] for row in rows],colWidths=widths,repeatRows=1,hAlign='LEFT')
 t.setStyle(TableStyle([('BACKGROUND',(0,0),(-1,0),colors.HexColor('#dfedef')),('VALIGN',(0,0),(-1,-1),'TOP'),('LINEBELOW',(0,0),(-1,0),.7,colors.HexColor('#99b4ba')),('LINEBELOW',(0,1),(-1,-1),.3,colors.HexColor('#d5e0e4')),('TOPPADDING',(0,0),(-1,-1),7),('BOTTOMPADDING',(0,0),(-1,-1),7)]));story.append(t);story.append(Spacer(1,10))
def new(title):story.append(PageBreak());p(title,'Heading1')
p('AA / 19 OCTOBER 2026','SmallAA');p('Can four air motors cool an outdoor seat?','Title')
p('<b>Conditional yes.</b> The proposed source is consistent with the first law at the catalogue loaded operating point. A 20°C occupied zone remains unproved. It depends on shaft loading, inlet temperature, heat pickup and ambient-air exchange.')
tbl([['Reference quantity','Calculated value','Status'],['Motor arrangement','4 in parallel','Assumed from the supplied environment'],['Air demand','3.888 m³/min atmospheric free air','Manufacturer consumption at maximum output'],['Mass flow','0.0776 kg/s','DOCX conversion: 19.4 g/s per motor'],['Shaft work extracted','3.36 kW total','Catalogue maximum; external load required'],['Motor exhaust / supply','-3.04°C / +0.96°C','Dry balance; 40°C inlet, +4 K duct gain'],['Sensible air-cooling capacity','2.27 kW vs 30°C ambient','Conditional enthalpy deficit; not skin cooling']], [136,145,226])
h('The architecture that can work')
p('Remote rental compressor → aftercooler, separator, dryer and filters → pressure-controlled air supply → four <b>loaded</b> LZB46 motors → short enlarged exhaust branches → cold collector → custom nozzle or control outlet → sheltered occupied region.')
p('Route shaft-load heat and diesel exhaust away from both the person and the cold path. All non-nozzle components remain off the shelf. A matched load assembly has not yet been selected.')
h('Four gates before a seat CFD result is credible')
p('1. Sustain the paired motor power and flow. 2. Keep compressed-air inlet at or below 40°C. 3. Verify the complete exhaust pressure loss. 4. Keep warm-air exchange below the target heat budget.')
p('<b>Current evidence:</b> manufacturer product page, exact motor manual, manufacturer rating guide, live compressor table and source DOCX. These support a mathematical screen. They do not guarantee refrigeration performance.','SmallAA')
new('1 / Source cooling requires shaft work')
eq('mdot*(h01 - h02) = Pshaft - Qmotor\nTmotor = Tin - (Pshaft-Qmotor)/(mdot*cp)\nTs = Tmotor + duct_gain\nQcold = mdot*cp*(Ta-Ts)')
p('Heat into the motor is positive. Temperatures represent recovered bulk states. The simplified model uses cp = 1006 J/(kg K). At the nominal mass flow, mdot·cp = 78.0656 W/K.')
p('At 40°C inlet, 3.36 kW extraction gives a 43.04 K bulk temperature reduction. The assumed 4 K path gain leaves 0.96°C supply air. Thus the document’s 1°C boundary is internally consistent, but conditional.')
tbl([['Extracted shaft work','Supply with prescribed +4 K path','Meaning'],['100% = 3.36 kW','0.96°C','Reference maximum-power pair'],['75% = 2.52 kW','11.72°C','Fixed-flow energy sensitivity only'],['50% = 1.68 kW','22.48°C','Fixed-flow energy sensitivity only']], [146,163,198])
p('Motor consumption changes with load and speed. These lower-power rows are not a motor curve. Free running does not extract rated external shaft work. Select a commercial generator/load or brake and speed control near 0.84 kW, 1270 rpm per motor.')
h('Small thermal margin at 1°C')
p('The 1°C supply target permits only <b>315 W total motor-plus-duct heat pickup</b>. The assumed +4 K duct gain already uses 312 W. An 8°C supply permits 862 W. Every extra 100 W adds 1.28 K; every 1 K inlet rise costs 78 W of cooling capacity.')
eq('Real duct: Ts = Ta+(Tmotor-Ta)*exp(-UA/(mdot*cp))')
p('The +4 K reference corresponds to UA ≈ 10.1 W/K. A fixed +4 K is a prescribed sensitivity, not a universal duct law. A warmer-than-ambient stream cools in a passive duct.')
h('Isentropic reference versus isenthalpic throttling')
p('At 6.3 bar gauge and 40°C inlet, the catalogue work/flow pair implies about 32% shaft isentropic efficiency. CoolProp dry-air EOS gives about -4.32°C recovered exhaust, versus -3.04°C in the constant-cp model. A regulator alone gives about 38.72°C. It cannot replace loaded expansion here.')
p('If all 3.36 kW of extracted work returns as heat to the same occupied zone, it cancels the work-driven cooling term. Keep that heat outside the control volume.','SmallAA')
new('2 / Compressor and exhaust network')
tbl([['Listed model','FAD at pressure','Four motors at rated point'],['XAS 38 / 48 / 58','2 / 2.5 / 3 m³/min at 7 bar','Insufficient continuous supply'],['XAS 68','3.6 m³/min at 7 bar on live page','Insufficient; brochure says 3.5'],['XAS 78','4.5 m³/min at 7 bar','15.7% bare margin'],['XAS 88','5.0 m³/min at 7 bar','28.6% bare margin'],['XAS 98','5.4 m³/min at 7 bar','38.9% bare margin'],['XAHS 38 / XATS 68','2 at 12 / 3.6 at 10.3 bar','Higher pressure does not fix low flow']], [121,185,201])
p('<b>XAS 78 is the first listed flow candidate.</b> It barely clears an assumed 15% flow allowance. Dryer purge, leaks, hot-weather derating and pressure losses need a budget. XAS 88 offers more flow margin. These are screening candidates, not purchase selections.')
p('7 bar supply leaves about 0.7 bar above the catalogue motor point for supply treatment and distribution losses. Compressor FAD and motor atmospheric-flow reference conditions must be harmonised. The brochure and live page differ for some smaller models.')
h('The 35°C case needs a supply correction')
p('The exact motor manual limits <b>both surrounding and inlet compressed air to 40°C</b>. Ambient 35°C plus a 10 K aftercooler rise gives 45°C and violates that limit. Require a final inlet approach of at most 5 K at 35°C. An aftercooler and water separator do not establish a +3°C pressure dew point; a dryer is a separate requirement.')
h('The small exhaust branches matter')
tbl([['Per-motor branch ID','Speed near 1 atm','1 m straight friction loss'],['16 mm','74.9 m/s','≈ 4.52 kPa'],['32 mm','18.7 m/s','≈ 141 Pa'],['40 mm','12.0 m/s','≈ 46 Pa'],['50 mm','7.7 m/s','≈ 15 Pa']], [157,160,190])
p('Screen assumes Darcy f = 0.02; detailed sizing needs a compressible network. The 16 mm kinetic head is about 3.6 kPa, but not all head is irreversible loss. Expand promptly, use short larger branches, and include bends, collectors and silencers. The final 150 mm outlet’s 7.5 Pa kinetic head does not establish negligible motor back pressure.','SmallAA')
new('3 / Wind and cold-air capture set the zone limit')
eq('(Cz+W)*Tzone = Cz*Ts + W*Ta + L\nCz = capture*mdot*cp; W = mwarm*cp\nDelta = [Cz*(Ta-Ts)-L]/(Cz+W)')
p('L includes the person, heated panels, absorbed solar heat and any shaft-load heat entering the region. The model is dry, steady and uniform. It does not predict torso or neck temperature separately.')
p('<b>At 30°C ambient, 0.96°C supply, full capture and 100 W net load:</b> a 20°C uniform zone requires warm-air exchange ≤ 0.1378 kg/s, or <b>0.1184 m³/s at ambient conditions</b>. At half capture the allowed volume drops to 0.0549 m³/s. Adding 500 W of panel/solar heat reduces the full-capture allowance to 0.0757 m³/s.')
eq('m_warm <= [capture*mdot*cp*(Ttarget-Ts)-L]\n          /[cp*(Ta-Ttarget)]')
img=Image(str(R/'results/viability-boundaries.png'),width=507,height=203);story.append(img);story.append(Spacer(1,8))
p('A crude wind model uses mwarm = rho·Cd·A·Vwind. With Cd = 1, the target requires effective exchange area ≤ 0.237 m² at 0.5 m/s or ≤ 0.118 m² at 1 m/s. These are <b>exchange-model limits, not seat opening dimensions</b>. Direction, shielding and recirculation require 3D CFD.')
p('With one effective m², the same model gives about 26.7°C at 0.5 m/s and 28.3°C at 1 m/s. A cold pool below the seat does not prove cooling at torso height.')
p('For a uniform transient volume, tau = M·cp/(Cz+W). Continuous supply replaces cold air. No fixed 0.5-second lifetime follows. A buffer changes peak delivery and duty, not average cooling production.','SmallAA')
new('4 / Controls, custom nozzles and CFD gates')
tbl([['Outlet control','Reference speed','Important limitation'],['A: 0.5 m² plate, 20% open','0.12 m/s face; 0.60 in holes','Hole geometry and resistance unknown'],['B: 150 mm open duct','3.41 m/s','Direction and ambient entrainment'],['C: four 70 mm nozzles','3.92 m/s','Local speeds differ at body'],['D: 80/20 hybrid','0.48 plate holes; 3.07 neck','Split requires branch balancing'],['Custom candidates','Match total open area to flow','Directional slots, low-loss diffusers, hybrids']], [165,143,199])
p('Retain A-D as controls. Reuse earlier nozzle concepts, then rescale. A 28 mm outlet per motor gives about 24.5 m/s. The old 8 mm throat flags compressible flow and back pressure at this source flow. Previous small-vortex CFD does not transfer.')
p('A possible custom CAD seed is two 150 × 50 mm slots, total area 0.015 m², at about 4 m/s. This defines a flow area only. It is not a tested optimum or a fitted assembly.')
h('What to change in the input document')
p('<b>Source:</b> label 1°C as a conditional operating point. Add the shaft load, motor-body heat budget, inlet-temperature limit, dryer and full exhaust network. Treat 5% turbulence as an assumption.')
p('<b>Moisture:</b> enthalpy-conserving mixing checks support no fog for the stated dry source and 55% ambient RH. Peak mixture RH is about 69% for 30°C/1°C, and below 92% across the sampled range. This does not establish freedom from internal icing, liquid carryover or cold-surface condensation.')
p('<b>Person:</b> choose a 100 W heat-input model or fixed 34°C skin temperature with predicted heat flow. Do not fix both independently on the same boundary. Separate air temperature, air speed, skin heat transfer and comfort claims.')
h('Next computational sequence')
p('1. Couple commercial source/load candidates to a thermal and pressure network. Reject infeasible source states. 2. Build the seat and collector CAD. 3. Run variable-density, buoyant 3D still-air cases. 4. Add 0.5/1 m/s wind from front and side. 5. Add solar/panel loads and source uncertainties. 6. Iterate outlet shape and location using torso/neck temperature, source capture, heat removal and pressure loss.')
p('Check mesh/time-step sensitivity, conservation and stable statistics. Compare turbulence and scalar-diffusion choices. Existing axisymmetric constant-density jet CFD is insufficient for these seat cases. No new seat CFD was run for this first-step assessment.','SmallAA')
new('5 / Proofs, evidence and decisions')
h('Verified mathematical work')
p('<b>Six new Lean theorems compile successfully.</b> They check the source target inequality, zone deficit identity, zone target inequality, shaft-heat cancellation, four-motor flow threshold and a concrete reference certificate. The full model now has 41 printed axiom checks, using only standard Lean/mathlib foundations. No unproved placeholders or new physics axioms are used.')
p('The reference certificate assumes: 30°C ambient; 40°C inlet; 3.36 kW shaft extraction; 0.0776 kg/s; heat pickup ≤312.2624 W; full cold capture; warm-air flow ≤0.12 kg/s; and a 100 W net heat load. Given the steady balances, Lean proves zone temperature &lt;20°C. It does not prove that a real seat satisfies those assumptions.')
p('<b>13 numerical checks pass.</b> They cover mass conversion, torque/power consistency, source and zone energy closure, compressor threshold, EOS efficiency, shaft-heat return and humid mixing. EOS, psychrometrics, motor performance, wind and human comfort remain outside the formal proof.')
h('Decision from this assessment')
p('<b>Proceed with the loaded-motor concept as a computational candidate.</b> Do not accept an unladen motor, an unspecified 2–5 m³/min rental unit, or a free choice of 1°C inlet in CFD as a complete system definition. A cold buffer is not the first design lever. Prioritise the work sink, air treatment, exhaust collector and wind shelter.')
p('Energy efficiency remains unestablished. XAS 78 has a 33 kW engine nameplate versus 2.27 kW reference cooling. The 6.9% ratio is not fuel COP. Actual fuel use, part-load behaviour, drying power and shaft-work recovery need separate assessment.')
h('Inputs still needed for the next CFD step')
p('Seat dimensions and openings; actual rental unit and treatment options; commercial motor-load assembly; collector/duct layout; and precise torso/neck sampling regions. No hardware measurement is required to start those models, but these choices must be explicit.')
h('Reproduce and inspect')
p('Editable derivation: FIRST-PRINCIPLES.txt. Calculations: assess.py. Results: results/assessment.json. Numerical checks: results/verification.json. Formal source: ../formal-model/AAThermo/MotorSeat.lean. Build and proof hashes: ../formal-model/build.log and proof-verification.json. The project overview links all artifacts.','SmallAA')
h('Primary sources')
